#: ../marketing/templates/pages/index.tmpl:81
msgid "<code>docker compose up</code> brings up openvoxserver, openvoxdb, Postgres and the console together, so you can point a test agent at it and see your own nodes appear before committing to anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../marketing/gen/main.go:58
msgid "A Puppet Enterprise console equivalent for OpenVox: node inventory, classification, code deployment, orchestration, package and vulnerability tracking, and role-based access control - in a single Go binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../marketing/templates/pages/features/classification.tmpl:43
msgid "A node that has never checked in has no facts yet, so no fact-based rule can match it. Pin it to a group directly if it needs classification before its first run."
msgstr ""

#: ../marketing/templates/pages/features/security.tmpl:45
msgid "A node with no package inventory cannot be assessed, and the console says so rather than counting it as clean. \"Nothing known against it\" and \"never looked\" are different answers and appear differently."
msgstr ""

#: ../marketing/templates/pages/features/nodes.tmpl:46
msgid "A node's own page gathers its facts, its recent runs, the classes classification gave it, what it has installed and which vulnerabilities touch it — everything you want when one machine, rather than the fleet, is the question."
msgstr ""

#: ../marketing/templates/pages/features/access-control.tmpl:12
msgid "A role is a named list of permissions — read nodes, deploy code, run orchestration, manage vulnerability providers. Give a person one role or several. They see the parts of the console their roles cover, and nothing else: no buttons that fail when clicked."
msgstr ""

#: ../marketing/gen/main.go:98
msgid "Access control"
msgstr ""

